    "result_text": "Full suite green: **273 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented city title-casing on owner creation with existing-spelling reuse.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `NormalizeOwnerCity.java`: given the built owner and `OwnerRepository`, it scans existing owners for one whose city matches (case-insensitively). If found, it copies that owner's exact city spelling onto the new owner; otherwise it title-cases the requested city (each word's first letter uppercased, the rest lowercased). Follows the existing `EnsureOwnerUnique` pattern (`@Val Owner` + repository, same-owner guard).\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted a `normalizeCity` step between `defaultRegistrationDate` and `ensureUnique`, under the same `transaction` governance. Placing it before `assignCustomerCode` means the customer-code city grouping sees the canonical spelling, so all owners in a city stay consistent.\n\nThis satisfies both cp12 test cases: a lowercase `\"riverdale\"` is returned as `\"Riverdale\"`, and a second owner submitting the same city in a different case reuses the first owner's stored spelling.",
